// pdisp: touch and pen input of the Android device go to the virtual monitor only, never to another display (docs/touch.md).
// "PNP(PDI) pdisp PDISP0001" is the monitor's identity (make, model, serial) with the daemon's defaults; it does not depend on the connector name.
// Add `include "pdisp.kdl"` to your niri config, or paste the block into it.
input {
    touch {
        map-to-output "PNP(PDI) pdisp PDISP0001"
    }
    tablet {
        map-to-output "PNP(PDI) pdisp PDISP0001"
    }
}
